    num: "32",
    title: "Rat in a Maze Problem",
    tag: "Path Finding",
    category: "Backtracking",
    subtitle: "Right & Down Maze Path Counting",
    brief: `A Maze is given as N*N binary matrix of blocks. A rat starts from source (0,0) and has to reach destination (N-1, N-1).

The rat can move only in two directions: rightwards and downwards.

In the maze matrix, -1 means the block is a dead end and 0 means the block can be used in the path from source to destination.

Your task is to find the number of possible solutions for the rat to reach the destination.

Input Format:
First line contains number of rows i.e. N.
Next N lines contain N space-separated integers denoting the maze.

Constraints:
2 <= N <= 15

Output Format:
Print the number of solutions.`,
    inputFormat: "First line contains N. Next N lines contain N integers.",
    outputFormat: "Print the total count of valid paths from (0,0) to (N-1, N-1).",
    starterCode: `import java.util.Scanner;

class Result {
  public static int solveMaze(int maze[][], int size) {
    // Write your code here

  }
}

class Main {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
    if (!sc.hasNextInt()) return;
    int n = sc.nextInt();
    int[][] maze = new int[n][n];
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
        maze[i][j] = sc.nextInt();
      }
    }
    System.out.println(Result.solveMaze(maze, n));
  }
}`,
    solutionCode: `import java.util.Scanner;

class Result {
  static int countPaths(int[][] maze, int r, int c, int n) {
    if (r < 0 || r >= n || c < 0 || c >= n || maze[r][c] == -1) {
      return 0;
    }
    if (r == n - 1 && c == n - 1) {
      return 1;
    }
    return countPaths(maze, r + 1, c, n) + countPaths(maze, r, c + 1, n);
  }

  public static int solveMaze(int maze[][], int size) {
    if (maze == null || size <= 0 || maze[0][0] == -1 || maze[size - 1][size - 1] == -1) {
      return 0;
    }
    return countPaths(maze, 0, 0, size);
  }
}

class Main {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
    if (!sc.hasNextInt()) return;
    int n = sc.nextInt();
    int[][] maze = new int[n][n];
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
        maze[i][j] = sc.nextInt();
      }
    }
    System.out.println(Result.solveMaze(maze, n));
  }
}`,
    hints: [
