  q84_implement_dijkstras_algorithm: {
    id: "q84_implement_dijkstras_algorithm",
    num: "84",
    title: "Implement Dijkstra's Algorithm",
    tag: "Dijkstra's Algorithm",
    category: "Graphs",
    subtitle: "Single Source Shortest Path on Weighted Undirected Graph",
    image: "dijkstra_graph.png",
    brief: `Implement Dijkstra's shortest path algorithm.

Given a weighted, undirected and connected graph along with a starting vertex 'src'. You have to find the shortest distance from the starting vertex to every vertex in the graph, and return a list of integers denoting the shortest distance between each vertex and starting vertex src.

Input Format:
First line contains two space separated integers V, E denoting the number of vertices and edges in the graph.
Following E lines contain three space separated integers u, v, w denoting an undirected edge between u and v having weight w.
Last line contains an integers src, denoting the starting vertex.

Constraints:
1 <= V <= 100
0 <= E <= 1000
0 <= u, v, src < 100
1 <= w <= 10

Output Format:
Space separated integers denoting the shortest distance between each vertex and starting vertex 'src'.

Explanation:
As 0 is the starting point, so the shortest distance till 0 vertex would be zero.
• Shortest path from 0 to 1 is 0->2->1. Distance would be 7
• Shortest path from 0 to 2 is 0->2. Distance would be 3
• Shortest path from 0 to 3 is 0->2->1->3. Distance would be 9
• Shortest path from 0 to 4 is 0->2->4. Distance would be 5`,
    inputFormat: "First line: V E. Next E lines: u v w. Last line: src.",
    outputFormat: "Space separated integers denoting the shortest distance from src to all vertices 0..V-1.",
    starterCode: `import java.io.*;
import java.util.*;

class Result {
  /*     
   * Complete the 'shortestDistance' function below.
   * @params
   *   N -> number of vertices in the graph
   *   E -> number of edges in the graph
   *   edges -> 2D array of size E * 3, with E rows and 3 columns,
   *            where edges[i][0] and edges[i][1] denotes the 2 vertices having an undirected edge,
   *            and edges[i][2] denotes the weight that the edge carries
   *   src -> starting source vertex
   *
   * @return
   *   a list of integers denoting the shortest distance between each vertex and starting vertex 'src'.
   */
  
  public ArrayList<Integer> shortestDistance(int N, int E, int[][] edges, int src) {
    // Write your code here
    


  }
}

class Main {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
    if (!sc.hasNextInt()) return;
    int V = sc.nextInt();
    int E = sc.nextInt();
    int[][] edges = new int[E][3];
    for (int i = 0; i < E; i++) {
      edges[i][0] = sc.nextInt();
      edges[i][1] = sc.nextInt();
      edges[i][2] = sc.nextInt();
    }
    int src = sc.nextInt();
    Result res = new Result();
    ArrayList<Integer> dist = res.shortestDistance(V, E, edges, src);
    for (int i = 0; i < dist.size(); i++) {
      System.out.print(dist.get(i) + (i < dist.size() - 1 ? " " : ""));
    }
    System.out.println();
  }
}`,
    solution: `import java.io.*;
import java.util.*;

class Result {
  /*     
   * Complete the 'shortestDistance' function below.
   * @params
   *   N -> number of vertices in the graph
   *   E -> number of edges in the graph
   *   edges -> 2D array of size E * 3, with E rows and 3 columns,
   *            where edges[i][0] and edges[i][1] denotes the 2 vertices having an undirected edge,
   *            and edges[i][2] denotes the weight that the edge carries
   *   src -> starting source vertex
   *
   * @return
   *   a list of integers denoting the shortest distance between each vertex and starting vertex 'src'.
   */
  
  public ArrayList<Integer> shortestDistance(int N, int E, int[][] edges, int src) {
    List<List<int[]>> adj = new ArrayList<>();
    for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        adj.add(new ArrayList<>());
    }
    for (int i = 0; i < E; i++) {
        int u = edges[i][0];
        int v = edges[i][1];
        int w = edges[i][2];
        adj.get(u).add(new int[]{v, w});
        adj.get(v).add(new int[]{u, w});
    }

    int[] dist = new int[N];
    Arrays.fill(dist, Integer.MAX_VALUE);
    dist[src] = 0;

    PriorityQueue<int[]> pq = new PriorityQueue<>((a, b) -> a[1] - b[1]);
    pq.add(new int[]{src, 0});

    while (!pq.isEmpty()) {
        int[] top = pq.poll();
        int u = top[0];
        int d = top[1];

        if (d > dist[u]) continue;

        for (int[] edge : adj.get(u)) {
            int v = edge[0];
            int weight = edge[1];
            if (dist[u] + weight < dist[v]) {
                dist[v] = dist[u] + weight;
                pq.add(new int[]{v, dist[v]});
            }
        }
    }

    ArrayList<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();
    for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        result.add(dist[i]);
    }
    return result;
  }
}

class Main {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
    if (!sc.hasNextInt()) return;
    int V = sc.nextInt();
    int E = sc.nextInt();
    int[][] edges = new int[E][3];
    for (int i = 0; i < E; i++) {
      edges[i][0] = sc.nextInt();
      edges[i][1] = sc.nextInt();
      edges[i][2] = sc.nextInt();
    }
    int src = sc.nextInt();
    Result res = new Result();
    ArrayList<Integer> dist = res.shortestDistance(V, E, edges, src);
    for (int i = 0; i < dist.size(); i++) {
      System.out.print(dist.get(i) + (i < dist.size() - 1 ? " " : ""));
    }
    System.out.println();
  }
}`,
