    category: "Hashing",
    subtitle: "Find Length of Longest Consecutive Sequence in Array",
    brief: `Given an array of n positive integers. A subsequence is defined as an ordered subset of the array's elements having the same sequential ordering as the original array.

Write a program to find the length of the longest sub-sequence such that elements in the subsequence are consecutive integers, the consecutive numbers can be in any order. For example,

if input is {10, 101, 12, 13, 11, 14, 25}, then the longest consecutive subsequence is {10, 12, 13, 11, 14}, the output should be 5.

Expected time complexity: O(n)

Input Format:
First Line will contain an integer n denoting the total number of elements.
Second line contains n integers separated by space.

Output Format:
Print the length of the longest consecutive subsequence.

Constraints:
1 <= n <= 10^5
1 <= arr[i] <= 1000`,
    inputFormat: "First line: n. Second line: n space-separated integers.",
    outputFormat: "Print the length of the longest consecutive subsequence.",
    starterCode: `import java.util.*;
class Result {
