  q96_kth_distinct_element: {
    id: "q96_kth_distinct_element",
    num: "96",
    title: "Kth distinct element",
    tag: "Distinct Elements",
    category: "Hashing",
    subtitle: "Find K-th Non-Repeating Element in Order of Appearance",
    brief: `Given an array of positive integers, and an integer K, your task is to find the Kth distinct element present in the array. If there are fewer than K distinct elements, then return 0 as the answer.

A distinct element is an element which is present only once in an array.
Note: The elements are considered in the same order in which they appear in the array from left to right.

Example: arr[] = {6, 11, 4, 11, 9, 4}, K = 2
The only distinct elements in the array are 6 and 9.
6 appears first so it the 1st distinct element, and 9 appears second so it the 2nd distinct element in the array. Hence, for K=2 the answer is 9.

Input Format:
First line of input contains T = number of test cases.
Each test case contains three lines:
  First Line will contain an integer N, denoting the size of the array.
  Second line contains N integers separated by space, denoting the array elements.
  Third line contains an integer representing K.

Constraints:
1 <= T <= 10
1 <= N <= 10^5
1 <= arr[i] <= 10^5
1 <= K <= N

Output Format:
Print the Kth distinct element present in the array.`,
    inputFormat: "First line: T. Each testcase: N, followed by N integers, followed by K.",
    outputFormat: "Print the K-th distinct element, or 0 if fewer than K distinct elements.",
    starterCode: `import java.util.*;
class Result {
  static int kthDistinctElement(int arr[], int N, int K) {
    // Write your code here
    

  }
}
class Main
{
  public static void main(String[] args)
  {
    int t, n, i, k;
    Scanner s=new Scanner(System.in);
    if (!s.hasNextInt()) return;
    t=s.nextInt();
    while(t != 0)
    {
      n=s.nextInt();
      int[] a=new int[n];
      for(i=0;i<n;i++)
        a[i] = s.nextInt();
      k=s.nextInt();
      System.out.println(Result.kthDistinctElement(a, n, k));
      t--;
    }
  }
}`,
    solution: `import java.util.*;
class Result {
  static int kthDistinctElement(int arr[], int N, int K) {
    Map<Integer, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
    for (int x : arr) {
      map.put(x, map.getOrDefault(x, 0) + 1);
    }
    int distinctCount = 0;
    for (int x : arr) {
      if (map.get(x) == 1) {
        distinctCount++;
        if (distinctCount == K) return x;
      }
    }
    return 0;
  }
}
class Main
{
  public static void main(String[] args)
  {
    int t, n, i, k;
    Scanner s=new Scanner(System.in);
    if (!s.hasNextInt()) return;
    t=s.nextInt();
    while(t != 0)
    {
      n=s.nextInt();
      int[] a=new int[n];
      for(i=0;i<n;i++)
        a[i] = s.nextInt();
      k=s.nextInt();
      System.out.println(Result.kthDistinctElement(a, n, k));
      t--;
    }
  }
}`,
